Chapter: Cdx6020Control

  cites Foreword chapter Console

Section: Body

  mutable Cell = record { n : Integer }

  Pair = record { a : Integer, b : Integer }

 HAZARD: field a mutates c, field b is evaluated AFTER and reads c.
 CDX6020 must fire here.

  hazard : Cell -> Pair
  hazard (c) = Pair { a = (__record-set c "n" 5).n, b = c.n }

 SAFE: the read of c comes FIRST, so the write cannot be seen by it.
 CDX6020 must NOT fire here.

  safe : Cell -> Pair
  safe (c) = Pair { a = c.n, b = (__record-set c "n" 5).n }

 HAZARD THROUGH A LIST, which is the arm that separates the two traversals.
 The read of c sits inside a list literal, and until 2026-09-08 the search for
 it stopped at AApplyExpr, ABinaryExpr, AIfExpr, ALetExpr, AMatchExpr's
 scrutinee and AFieldAccess, answering False for every other variant. So this
 is the same hazard as the first one and CDX6020 could not see it. It must
 fire here, and an arm that only repeats the first hazard cannot tell a
 complete traversal from a partial one.

  hazard-in-list : Cell -> Pair
  hazard-in-list (c) = Pair { a = (__record-set c "n" 5).n, b = list-length [c.n] }

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((hazard (Cell { n = 1 })).b))
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((safe (Cell { n = 1 })).a))
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((hazard-in-list (Cell { n = 1 })).b))
  end

